### What is carried

Fifteen files, 7,249 lines, 274,966 bytes:

    barriers.cuh   defines.h     mha.cuh      mha_components.cuh   mma.cuh
    cuda_hint.cuh  hostUtils.h   mha.h        mha_stdheaders.cuh   platform.h
    ldgsts.cuh     specDec.h     mhaUtils.cuh utils.cuh            utils.h

Not carried, and deliberately: `gmma.cuh`, `gmma_impl.cuh`, `mha_sm90.cu`,
`mla_sm120.cu`, `mla_sm120.cuh`, `tensorMap.cpp`, `tensorMap.h`, `tma.h`,
`xqa_wrapper.cu`. The first five are sm_90/sm_120 TMA and GMMA paths this
crate does not build; the rest are host code -- a `.cpp` and a `.cu` wrapper
whose job (tensor-map construction, kernel launch) is Rust's here, in
`driver-cuda/src/fire/xqa.rs`.

### What was changed

**Three of the fifteen files differ from upstream at all; the other twelve are
byte-identical.** Across those three: 56 lines added, 5 replaced, net +51.

  * `mha.cu` is carried as **`mha.cuh`**. It is a rename and nothing else.
    This crate holds no translation units -- a `.cu` is an ahead-of-time TU
    for nvcc and there is no nvcc here -- and the rename is free because
    nothing includes it by its upstream name. Every `mha.cu:N` citation in
    this repo is against upstream; `mha.cuh:N` means our copy. The file's own
    header note gives the offset both ways and it is arithmetic, not memory:
    3,093 - 3,051 = 42.
  * One `#ifndef GENERATE_CUBIN` guard, around the host tail of `mha.cuh`
    (`configureKernel`, `launchMHAFlashInfer` -- `cudaMemcpyFromSymbol`,
    `cudaFuncSetAttribute`, `cudaLaunchKernelEx`). Upstream guards its *own*
    host launcher `launchMHA` exactly this way at `mha.cu:2820`; this tail is
    FlashInfer's downstream addition and they never guarded it. The guarded
    body's replacement is `driver-cuda/src/fire/xqa.rs`.
  * Five `#include` spellings made tree-relative -- `"mma.cuh"` and
    `"utils.cuh"` become `"attn/xqa/mma.cuh"` and `"attn/xqa/utils.cuh"` in
    `mha.cuh`, `mhaUtils.cuh` and `mha_components.cuh`. This is the one change
    forced by carrying two upstream trees at once: FlashInfer *also* has an
    `mma.cuh` and a `utils.cuh`, NVRTC has a single flat include namespace
    keyed on the literal directive string, and a bare `"utils.cuh"` from XQA
    would otherwise resolve to FlashInfer's. Those five are the only bare
    spellings either tree shares; the other nine XQA directives name files
    FlashInfer does not have and were left alone.
  * 48 `// PIE:` marker lines across the same three files, in the same fixed
    form used on the FlashInfer side. `grep -rn "// PIE:" csrc/src/attn/xqa/`
    finds all 48.

Note the shape of the difference from the FlashInfer side of this document:
there, the changes are 35 `#ifndef __CUDACC_RTC__` guards; here there are
**none**. XQA was written to be compiled as a cubin -- it carries upstream's
own `GENERATE_CUBIN` switch for exactly that -- so the JIT needed one guard
where FlashInfer's host-facing headers needed thirty-three. Diffing XQA
against a fresh checkout is correspondingly cheap.


